#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:15
msgid "pio test"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:17
msgid "Helper command for local :ref:`unit_testing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:19
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:22
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:29
#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:182
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:31
msgid ""
"Run project tests on host (local) machine using PlatformIO :ref:"
"`unit_testing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:34
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:41
msgid ""
"Process specified project environment. Multiple environments are allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:46
msgid ""
"Process only test suites whose path relative to the :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_test_dir` matches the specified pattern. See documentation "
"for the :ref:`projectconf_test_filter` project configuration option for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:51
msgid "Example, ``pio test --filter \"test_common\" -f \"native/*\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:56
msgid ""
"Ignore test suites whose path relative to the :ref:"
"`projectconf_pio_test_dir` matches the specified pattern. See documentation "
"for the :ref:`projectconf_test_ignore` project configuration option for more "
"details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:61
msgid "For example, ``pio test --ignore \"embedded/*\" -i \"test_suite[13]\"``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:66
msgid ""
"A port that is intended for firmware uploading. To list available ports "
"please use the :ref:`cmd_device_list` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:69
msgid ""
"If the upload port is not specified, PlatformIO will try to detect it "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:74
msgid ""
"A Serial/UART port that PlatformIO uses as a communication interface between "
"PlatformIO Unit Test Engine and target device. To list available ports "
"please use :ref:`cmd_device_list` command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:78
msgid ""
"If test port is not specified, PlatformIO will try to detect it "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:83
msgid ""
"Specify the path to the project directory. By default, ``--project-dir`` is "
"equal to a current working directory (``CWD``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:89
msgid "Process project with a custom :ref:`projectconf`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:94
msgid "Skip the building stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:99
msgid "Skip the uploading stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:104
msgid "Skip the testing stage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:109
msgid ""
"Disable software reset via ``Serial.DTR/RST`` before test running. In this "
"case, need to press the \"reset\" button manually after firmware uploading."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:113
msgid ""
"If the board does not support software reset via ``Serial.DTR/RTS`` you "
"should add >2 seconds delay before ``UNITY_BEGIN()``. We need that time to "
"establish a ``Serial`` communication between the host machine and the target "
"device. See :ref:`unit_testing`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:121
msgid ""
"Set initial ``RTS`` line state for Serial Monitor (``0`` or ``1``), default "
"``1``. We use it to gather test results via a Serial connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:127
msgid ""
"Set initial ``DTR`` line state for Serial Monitor (``0`` or ``1``), default "
"``1``. We use it to gather test results via a Serial connection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:133
msgid ""
"Pass an extra argument to the testing program. Multiple arguments are "
"allowed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:135
msgid ""
"If you need to pass extra arguments permanently per a testing environment, "
"please take a look at the :ref:`projectconf_test_testing_command`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:138
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:149
msgid ""
"List project tests without processing. The :option:`pio test --json-output-"
"path` or :option:`pio test --junit-output-path` options can be used for "
"dumping available test suites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:156
msgid ""
"Return the output in `JSON <http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSON>`__ format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:161
msgid ""
"Generate a unit testing report in the `JSON <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"JSON>`__ format and save it to the specified path. If the only folder path "
"is provided, the file name will be generated automatically. Please note that "
"the parent folder must exist before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../core/userguide/cmd_test.rst:169
msgid ""
"The same as :option:`pio test --json-output-path` but generates a report in "
"the `JUnit XML <https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/developer-for-zos/14.1.0?"
"topic=formats-junit-xml-format>`_ format."
msgstr ""

